# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8-262k window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8-262k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1 is the STAGE-2 image: built by SB9 from the commit
# that records the stage-1 evidence (packed_any_evidence_tp4_262144.json and ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json at their pins), WITHOUT a baked default: the
# eight-seat 131k image tp4-serve-8 stays what ships until the owner says otherwise. Each job names its profile explicitly. A commit that changes a file the
# image carries needs a new SB9 build and a new tag in every template.
# M9b (STOP, memory, the one that sizes the pool): EIGHT prompts of 157,000 tokens on the 262k traffic profile. Each reserves 2,711 blocks, 8 x 2,711 = 21,688 of
# the provisional 21,759 usable: the pool is FULL and nothing holds. READ: the floor (free less the stranded bytes less the estimate) at least 1.0 GB per chip at
# eight live seats, F8 in the pool formula blocks = 16,416 + floor((F8 - 1.0 GB - 0.067 GB) / 557,056 bytes) - the provisional 21,760 needs F8 of about 4.05 GB; the
# trace region's largest free block at least 44 MB. If F8 reads lower, the FINAL num-gpu-blocks-override is the formula's value at the measured F8 and the image is
# REBUILT (tp4-262k8-2, a new SB9 build and a new tag in every template) before L9b. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; attach 15-40 min; eight 157k prefills one
# fresh prompt at a time 40-60 min; the short arm 5 min: 60 / 75 / 90 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k
C2_GATE_PLAN=memory
C2_GATE_MEMORY_PROMPT=157000
C2_GATE_JIT=record
